        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 66-year-old male admitted on 22/06/2026 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and received appropriate patient education regarding his condition and inhaler technique. He responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. He is discharged in stable condition and I kindly ask you to continue monitoring his COPD management and ensure follow-up spirometry in due course. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
